infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Validate & reject vs sanitize & mutate
  desc Two ways to meet hostile input at the boundary — parse, don't validate
  compares
    - label Validate & reject (parse)
      children
        - label Yes/no — does it match the schema?
          desc Asserts type, range, length, allowlist as one binary check at the door
        - label Rejects invalid input with a 400
          desc Nothing is silently rewritten; bad input never proceeds
        - label Yields one typed, trusted value
          desc Downstream code can assume validity — no re-checking needed
    - label Sanitize & mutate (strip)
      children
        - label Rewrites input to make it safe
          desc Strips or escapes characters instead of refusing the request
        - label A blocklist in disguise
          desc Only catches patterns you foresaw; double-encoding and unicode lookalikes slip through
        - label Leaves data wrong, maybe still dangerous
          desc Code runs on bytes the caller never sent — which hides bugs
theme
  palette #14b8a6 #f43f5e
